(b). Create required directories for the patches and install.
[root@caoradbauto01 ~] mkdir /u01
[root@caoradbauto01 ~] chown oracle:oinstall /u01
[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p  /u01/app/
[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p /u01/app/oracle/software
[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p /u01/app/oraInventory
[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p /u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/logs
[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p /u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/keystore
[oracle@caoradbauto01 ~]$ mkdir -p /u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/patches


(c). Create a config file to fetch patches

vi get-patches.cfg
global.global_log_dir=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/logs
global.keystore=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/keystore
global.folder=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/patches

patch1.platform=LINUX.X64
patch1.patch=RU:19.32,OPATCH,OJVM

In this configuration, I am using RU 19.32, the latest OPatch version, and the 19.32 OJVM update. Any compatible and officially released patches can be included alongside the Release Update.

(d). AutoUpgrade requires MOS credentials to be stored in its keystore in order to download patches from MyOracleSupport. The steps to create and configure the keystore are outlined below.

***************************************************************************************************************************
Create Autoupgrade Keystore
****************************************************************************************************************************

# Create a config file to create keystore. We use the same get-patches.cfg which we have created in Step 3

# Execute the command below to load the password. The tool will first ask you to create a password for encrypting the keystore, and this password does not need to match your MOS credentials.
[oracle@caoradbauto01 software]$ java -jar autoupgrade.jar -config get-patches.cfg -patch -load_password
Processing config file ...

Starting AutoUpgrade Patching Password Loader - Type help for available options
Creating new AutoUpgrade Patching keystore - Password required
Enter password:<Enter a password which will encrypt MOS Credentails in Keystore> 
Enter password again: <Enter a password which will encrypt MOS Credentails in Keystore>
AutoUpgrade Patching keystore was successfully created

# Add MOS Credentails to the Keystore.

MOS> add -user <MOS Login Username/Email>
Enter your secret/Password: <MOS Password>
Re-enter your secret/Password: <MOS Password>

# Save the changes. 
MOS> save
Select auto-login mode for the AutoUpgrade Patching keystore [YES|NO|SHARED]: YES

# Exit from the Keystore configuration.
MOS> exit

AutoUpgrade Patching Password Loader finished - Exiting AutoUpgrade Patching

