***************************************************************************************************************************
Install Oracle DB Home 
****************************************************************************************************************************
5. Install Oracle DB Home 

Since we have already downloaded software we can start the install.

(a). Create a AutoUprade config file to install software.

vi install-home.cfg

global.global_log_dir=/u01/app/oracle/software/autoupgrade/logs
install1.patch=RU:19.32,OPATCH,OJVM
install1.folder=/u01/app/oracle/software
install1.target_home=/u01/app/19.32.0/db
install1.home_settings.oracle_base=/u01/app/oracle
install1.home_settings.edition=EE
install1.home_settings.inventory_location=/u01/app/oraInventory
install1.download=no


(b). The following command initiates the installation as a background job and simultaneously opens the console, where you can run helpful commands—for example, viewing the status of jobs and tasks.

